From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:11:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Return -ENOBUFS when the channel switch request does not fit

nl80211_switch_channel() stores the result of nl80211_put_freq_params()
in ret within the condition that adds the first attributes. If adding a
later attribute of that condition fails, the function frees the message
and returns 0. hostapd_switch_channel() then sets csa_in_progress for a
channel switch that the driver never received.

Return -ENOBUFS for a failure to add an attribute, as before the
conversion from the NLA_PUT macros.

Fixes: a862e4a38fa2 ("nl80211: Continue getting rid of NLA_PUT* macro use")

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -12501,15 +12501,20 @@
 
 	if (!(msg = nl80211_bss_msg(bss, 0, NL80211_CMD_CHANNEL_SWITCH)) ||
 	    nla_put_u32(msg, NL80211_ATTR_CH_SWITCH_COUNT,
-			settings->cs_count) ||
-	    (ret = nl80211_put_freq_params(msg, &settings->freq_params, bss)) ||
-	    (settings->block_tx &&
+			settings->cs_count))
+		goto fail;
+
+	ret = nl80211_put_freq_params(msg, &settings->freq_params, bss);
+	if (ret)
+		goto error;
+
+	if ((settings->block_tx &&
 	     nla_put_flag(msg, NL80211_ATTR_CH_SWITCH_BLOCK_TX)) ||
 	    (drv->nlmode == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT && drv->mesh_handle_dfs &&
 	     nla_put_flag(msg, NL80211_ATTR_HANDLE_DFS)) ||
 	    (settings->link_id != NL80211_DRV_LINK_ID_NA &&
 	     nla_put_u8(msg, NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID, settings->link_id)))
-		goto error;
+		goto fail;
 
 	/* beacon_after params */
 	ret = set_beacon_data(msg, &settings->beacon_after, false);
